omarchy-theme-bg-current title-cases the background's file name with perl
working on bytes, so in a UTF-8 name a letter after an accented one counted
as a word start: "02-über-städte.jpg" showed as "üBer StäDte". Decode the
name as UTF-8 whatever the locale, with U+FFFD for bytes that are not UTF-8
(perl -CSD would die on them and print nothing), and write UTF-8: it shows
as "Über Städte". ASCII names come out as before (test_omarchy_theme_bg.py).
Proposed upstream in omacom/omarchy#14865; remove once the pinned Omarchy
includes it.

--- a/bin/omarchy-theme-bg-current
+++ b/bin/omarchy-theme-bg-current
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 BACKGROUND_PATH=$(readlink -f "$HOME/.local/state/omarchy/current/background" 2>/dev/null)
 
 if [[ -n $BACKGROUND_PATH ]]; then
-  basename -- "$BACKGROUND_PATH" | perl -pe 's/\.[^.]+$//; s/^\d+-//; s/-/ /g; s/\b(\w)/\U$1/g'
+  basename -- "$BACKGROUND_PATH" | perl -CO -MEncode=decode -pe '$_ = decode("UTF-8", $_); s/\.[^.]+$//; s/^\d+-//; s/-/ /g; s/\b(\w)/\U$1/g'
 else
   echo "Unknown"
 fi
